Accept strict OOXML relationship types as well as transitional ones.

ECMA-376 defines two namespace families. Transitional is what Excel writes by
default and roots relationship types at

  http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/

Strict -- the ISO/IEC 29500 variant, written when Excel is asked for "Strict
Open XML Spreadsheet" -- roots them at

  http://purl.oclc.org/ooxml/officeDocument/relationships/

main_sheet_get_rels_expat_callback_element_start compared against the
transitional spelling only, so for a strict workbook the worksheet, shared
string and styles relationships never matched. sheetfile, sharedstringsfile
and stylesfile were all left NULL.

The failure was silent, which is what makes it worth a patch rather than a
note. Listing sheets kept working, because that reads xl/workbook.xml
directly and needs no relationship. Opening a worksheet then succeeded and
produced nothing: read_xlsx() returned a data frame with no columns and no
rows, with no condition raised anywhere. Apache POI's corpus carries four such
files and all four were recorded as reading successfully.

reltype_is() matches the base case-insensitively and compares the remainder,
so exactly these two families are accepted. Testing only the last path
component would have been shorter and would accept a "worksheet" relationship
from any vocabulary at all, which is tested against.

Content types are not affected: a strict workbook declares the same ones a
transitional workbook does, which is why iterate_files_by_contenttype() and
the sheet listing built on it never needed changing.

Origin: written for zuxlsx. Not upstream.
Applies to xlsxio 0.2.36 with 0001 through 0005 already applied.
--- a/lib/xlsxio_read.c
+++ b/lib/xlsxio_read.c
@@ -942,6 +942,52 @@
